<http://data.silknow.org/object/6c31c6dd-ef6d-3422-971d-b011598b952c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Various silk stiches in brown, green, blue, red, yellow, black, beige and white on wool ground. The sampler has a central moral text in purple stitching, which is surrounded by floral, butterfly and crown decoration. At the bottom of the sampler are two human figures - a standing male, presumably a shepherd as he has sheep at his feet, as well as a woman seated holding a staff. There is a floral, rose shaped border. Made by Mary Grace, aged twelve in 1797."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6c31c6dd-ef6d-3422-971d-b011598b952c> .

